          Most weed killer disappointment comes from one mistake: buying the wrong type. A product that clears a gravel driveway for a year will scorch a bare patch in your lawn that takes a season to grow back. A product safe on turf will barely dent a woody vine. After a full season of side-by-side spraying, here is what each type actually does — and the seven products that did it best.
